# Cloudflare response headers for every served asset + prerendered page.
# This is the ONLY layer that reaches the prerendered pages (they are served by
# the asset layer, not the Worker), so the site's baseline security headers live
# here. The Worker-served routes (/, /api/*) get the same set from src/middleware.ts.
#
# CSP is deliberately conservative so it can't break the site: it restricts only
# object/base (which the site never uses) and does NOT constrain script/style —
# adding those would require nonces/hashes for the inline theme, GA, and JSON-LD.
# frame-ancestors is intentionally omitted so the /embed/ widget stays framable;
# clickjacking of a stateless preview tool is low-impact.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'
